<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<handout>
    <title>Sets And Notation</title>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>
            What is a Set?
            What Are the Symbols
            <m>\in, \notin, \subseteq, \subset, \not\subseteq, = ?</m>
        </title>

        <p>
            There's a lot of notation that comes with sets!
        </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <definition>
        <statement>
            <p>
                A <term>
                set
            </term> is an unordered
                collection of distinct objects which are called
                <term>
                elements
            </term>.
            </p>

            <p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            If <m>x</m> is an element of a set <m>S</m>, we
                            write <m>x\in S</m>.
                            This is read <q> <m>x</m> in <m>S</m> </q>.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            If <m>x</m> is not an element of a set <m>S</m>, we
                            write <m>x\notin S</m>.
                            This is read
                            <q> <m>x</m> is not in <m>S</m>
                                </q>.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            If every element of <m>A</m> is also an element of
                            <m>B</m> then <m>A</m> is a subset of <m>B</m>,
                            denoted <m>A\subseteq B</m> and read
                            <q> <m>A</m> is a subset of <m>B</m> </q>.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            If <m>A\subseteq B</m> and <m>A\neq B</m>, then we
                            write <m>A \subset B</m> and we say
                            <q> <m>A</m> is a
                                proper subset of <m>B</m> </q>.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            If <m>A</m> is not a subset of <m>B</m> then we
                            write <m>A\not\subseteq B</m> and say
                            <q> <m>A</m> is not a subset of <m>B</m> </q>.
                            This means there exists an <m>x\in A</m> such that
                            <m>x\notin B</m>.
                        </p>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <p>
                            If <m>A</m> and <m>B</m> have the exact same
                            elements, we write <m>A=B</m>.
                            This is read as <q> <m>A</m> equals <m>B</m> </q>.
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </definition>

    <activity workspace=".75in">
        <title>Set Relationships</title>

        <introduction>
            <p>
                Given the following information, what are all the possible set
                diagrams for the two sets?
                Can you find any other set relationships that must be true?
                (Think specifically about the complement sets as well.)
            </p>
        </introduction>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>A\subseteq B</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>C\cap D = \emptyset</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>J\subseteq K</m> and <m> K\subseteq J</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>N\not\subseteq M</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Every element of <m>G</m> is not an element of <m>H</m>.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </activity>

    <activity>
        <task workspace="1in">
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    Consider the set <m>A=\{1,2,3,\text{cat}, \star\}</m>.
                </p>
            </introduction>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        What are the elements of <m>A</m>?
                        How many are there?
                        (Later we'll refer to the number of elements in the set
                        as the <em>size</em> or the <em>cardinality</em>.)
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        List 3 different subsets of <m>A</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </task>

        <task workspace="1in">
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    Consider the set <m>B=\{1,2,3,\{4,9\},7\}</m>.
                </p>
            </introduction>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        What are the elements of <m>B</m>?
                        How many are there?
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        List 3 different subsets of <m>B</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Which of the following is correct to say:
                        <m>\{4,9\}\in B</m> or <m>\{4,9\}\subseteq B</m>?
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </task>

        <task workspace=".5in">
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    Let <m>A = \{1, \{2, 3\}\}</m>.
                    Decide whether each of the following statements is true or
                    false and briefly explain.
                </p>
            </introduction>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m>1\in A</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m>1\subseteq A</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m>\{1\} \in A</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m>\{2,3\}\in A</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m>\{2,3\} \subseteq A</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </task>

        <task workspace=".2in">
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    Let <m>A = \{ \ldots, -6, -3, 0, 3, 6, \ldots \}</m>,
                    <m>B = \{12, 24, 36 \}</m>, and <m>C = \{1, 2, 3\}</m>.
                    Which of the following statements are true?
                </p>
            </introduction>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> 9 \in A</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> 2\in C</m> and <m> 2\in A </m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> 5\notin A</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> 12\subseteq A</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> B \subseteq A</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> A \subseteq B</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> C\not\subseteq A</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> B=C</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> \{3\} \subseteq A</m> and <m> 3\subseteq C</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </task>

        <task workspace=".2in">
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    Fill in all of the symbols that apply from the list that
                    apply:
                    <m>\in, \notin, \subseteq, \subset, \not\subseteq, = </m>
                </p>
            </introduction>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> \{1\} </m> <fillin characters="10"/> <m> \{1,2\}</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> 1 </m> <fillin characters="10"/> <m> \{1,2\}</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> \{1\} </m> <fillin characters="10"/>
                        <m> \{\{1\},\{2\}\}</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> \{2,1\} </m> <fillin characters="10"/>
                        <m> \{1,2\}</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> 1 </m> <fillin characters="10"/> <m> \{\{1\},2\}</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> 2 </m> <fillin characters="10"/> <m> \{\{1\},2\}</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> \{1\} </m> <fillin characters="10"/>
                        <m> \{\{1\},2\}</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> \{2\} </m> <fillin characters="10"/>
                        <m> \{\{1\},2\}</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <m> \{1,2 \} </m> <fillin characters="10"/>
                        <m> \{\{1\},2\}</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </task>

        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    (If time:) Challenge Question 1: Can an object ever be both
                    an element and a subset of the same set?
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    (If time:) Challenge Question 2: How many subsets are there
                    of the set <m>\{1,2\}</m>?
                    Of the set <m>\{1,2,3\}</m>?
                    How many subsets do you think there will be of the set
                    <m>\{1,2,3,\dots, n\}</m> for <m>n\in\mathbb{N}</m>?
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </activity>
</handout>